---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
	title="About Us — Cute Timer | Cute Pomodoro Timer for Studying"
	description="Learn about Cute Timer, the free aesthetic pink pomodoro timer for studying and deep focus. Our story, our mission, and the tomato behind the cuteness."
	canonical="https://cutepomodorotimer.com/about/"
>
	<p class="eyebrow text-[var(--accent-ink)]">About the Cute Timer ♡</p>
	<h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-extrabold leading-snug text-ink sm:text-4xl">About Us</h1>
	<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body sm:text-base">
		Cute Timer is a free cute timer online built for students, remote workers, and anyone who wants deep focus
		without feeling like they're being graded. We believe productivity shouldn't be cold or punishing — it should
		feel like a cozy little ritual you actually look forward to.
	</p>

	<section class="mt-8">
		<h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-extrabold leading-snug text-ink sm:text-3xl">Why we built it</h2>
		<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-body sm:text-base">
			There are plenty of pomodoro timer apps out there, but most of them look like spreadsheets with a stopwatch.
			We wanted a cute pomodoro timer that pairs the classic Pomodoro Technique with soft pastel colors, gentle
			lo-fi music, a blushing tomato mascot, and little heart dots that celebrate every completed round. A timer
			you'd be happy to keep open all day on your desk.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-8">
		<h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-extrabold leading-snug text-ink sm:text-3xl">Our mission</h2>
		<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-body sm:text-base">
			Our mission is simple: make focused work feel friendly. Whether you need a 10 minute cute timer for a quick
			tidy-up, a 15 minute cute timer for flashcards, or a 30 minute cute timer for deep work, we want every
			session to end with a small sense of accomplishment — and a break you actually take.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-8">
		<h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-extrabold leading-snug text-ink sm:text-3xl">The little tomato</h2>
		<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-body sm:text-base">
			Our mascot is a tiny blushing tomato named Pommy. Pommy nods along while you focus, blinks during breaks,
			and celebrates when your round is complete. It's a gentle reminder that the original pomodoro was just a
			tomato-shaped kitchen timer — and that focus doesn't have to be serious all the time.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="mt-8">
		<h2 class="mb-3 text-2xl font-extrabold leading-snug text-ink sm:text-3xl">Our values</h2>
		<p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-body sm:text-base">
			Free forever. No sign-up, no ads, no accounts. Everything you set — your timer lengths, your to-do list,
			your music preference — is stored only in your own browser, so you stay in control. We build in the open,
			keep the interface simple, and always put your focus first.
		</p>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
